WEBVTT

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.160
You're really leaving?

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:17.370
Yeah.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.290
You said you'd help me find my killer.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.300
Sorry... but I can't do that.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.750
That task is too much for me.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.400
Because...

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.910
You're afraid that if you find 
my killer, you'll be killed, too?

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:39.220
That's what the
 Future-Revealing Mirror showed me.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.100
But don't worry. I couldn't do it,

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.870
but I'm sure the next person to 
move in here will grant your wish.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:29.650
<b><u>Episode 4</u></b>

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:29.650
Dreams and Ambitions and Denial and Attraction

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:32.030
I've been waiting for you, Juugo.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:37.920
Those two are going to make 
a deal with Ikkaku Shunjuu?

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.610
Yeah. Seems he plans to sell
 the cane for a hundred million yen.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.560
A hundred million?

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.240
As if we're gonna
 let them have their way.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.170
Hey, Juugo...

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:54.480
Do you think we'll be able to 
get the cane back from them?

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.500
What's wrong?

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.450
I'm... starting to feel scared.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.890
Would you hold me?

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.100
Okay. Come here.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.270
Who are you?

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.430
You're three centimeters taller than Juugo.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:30.230
Who notices a difference that small?

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.280
I'm a master detective, you see.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.740
Then I guess it's no
 surprise you figured me out.

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:39.620
Hey! You're the fake policeman from before!

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.530
Well, I can't tell you my name,

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.200
but in my business,
 I'm known as the Hundred-Faces

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.140
of the phantom thief troupe, Matsuri.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.120
I can't believe he was a real thief!

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:50.370
Falling for me now?

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:54.170
Yeah! I absolutely must apprehend you!

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:54.880
Huh?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.380
<i>Hey, hang on!
 We kidnapped Juugo-kun, you know!</i>

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.880
<i>So long, Juugo!
See you in the next life!</i>

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.350
<i>Ow, ow! You're gonna let him die?!</i>

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:04.480
<i>Stop right there!</i>

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.500
<i>Ow! That hurts!</i>

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.500
Everything's going according to plan.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:09.820
Now we only need to
 steal the treasure, right?

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:10.620
Right.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.850
Oh, here's the payment I promised.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:20.990
It's not a fake, right?

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.980
It's real.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:24.950
I see.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.520
Still, you surprised me.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.910
I never expected you
 to team up with Matsuri.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.600
I'm sorry! Forgive me!

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:33.950
I'm truly sorry!

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:38.500
Um, by the way, don't you 
want Nanana's Collection?

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:40.550
What do you mean?

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.990
I'm on my way to get
 back the Nanana's Collection

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.520
treasure that was here.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.050
I'd like your help.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.010
I'm grateful for
 your help, Yukihime-san.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.100
Did you choose us as your partners to

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.730
keep that master
 detective out of danger?

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.280
Of course not.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.980
I just didn't want her 
finding out who I really am.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.520
Would you take the girl?

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.460
Understood. Be careful.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:33.570
I never thought I'd end up fighting you.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.410
I also never thought

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:41.900
you'd want to sell a 
Nanana's Collection treasure.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.300
Of course, I would never do that.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:50.620
With this, I can grant any wish,
 as often as I please.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:54.330
It is the most powerful
 treasure of Nanana's Collection.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:59.790
Then what is it you really want?

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.450
To take over the world.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.360
What?

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.970
To take over the world!

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:11.530
My ambition is to rule this world.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:14.970
<i>He's an idiot.
 President Yuiga is an idiot.</i>

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:20.400
The first thing I'll do is manipulate 
Ikkaku Shunjuu with this cane,

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.640
and then this island is mine!

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:26.900
Um... anyway, I'm going
 to have to take that.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:31.370
Then I'll just get rid of you 
with the power of this cane.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.010
Burn!

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:39.290
<i>That's real magic!</i>

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:41.250
Freeze!

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.090
Impale!

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:51.950
Those quick movements of yours are a hassle.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:53.220
For now...

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:57.020
Stand motionless, Yama Juugo.

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:58.970
That's cheating!

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:01.090
This will hurt a bit.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:03.190
Blow away.

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:07.220
Ouch...

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:12.770
Blow away!

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:17.690
Now I see.

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:19.890
The force differs
 according to my mental image

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.290
and the volume of my voice?

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:23.770
That really hurt...

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:27.520
Thank you, Yama-kun.
 You helped me obtain excellent data.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:30.590
Come on... give it a rest!

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:33.310
Who do you think you are?

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:40.110
This island is just
 full of irritating people.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:43.650
"I wanna be a master detective," 
"I wanna take over the world"...

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.200
Are you all stupid?!

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:47.150
No one wants to hear
 that kind of nonsense!

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:50.140
It's so embarrassing, I could puke!

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:52.890
That's not something you
 shout out for the world to hear!

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:56.350
Just looking at people 
like you pisses me off!

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:58.700
Yama-kun, I pity you.

00:07:59.030 --> 00:07:59.950
What?!

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:03.180
What kind of
 ridiculous objection is that?

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.420
Are you saying it's
 embarrassing to have a dream?

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:09.120
Then what's true for you?

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:13.180
Does being the same as
 everyone else make you normal?

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:15.340
Does joining them in 
laughing down your nose

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:19.890
at those who struggle toward 
their goals make you normal?

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.890
Anyone who does that
 is the lowest form of scum!

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:25.300
People don't lose their dreams!

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:29.900
You're pissing me off.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:33.150
Let's have a contest to find out who's right.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:37.330
Will your dream come out on top,
 or my rotten ideals?

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:38.780
Let's have a test of endurance.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.420
Very well.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:44.290
Have a taste of my magic!

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.640
But I have to admit, you are tough.

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:09.920
My parents were sticklers for discipline.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.570
Even now,
 I never miss a day of training.

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:16.110
But if we continue,
 your life really will be on the line.

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:19.580
Go home and sleep,

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:21.300
Yama Juugo.

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:24.040
<i>That's how he's playing it?!</i>

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:29.250
What happened?

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:34.210
Finally ran out of energy, eh?

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:37.260
Wh-What is going on here?

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:40.000
You didn't know, did you?

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.290
That cane has a flaw.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:43.430
A flaw?

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.250
You said, "as often as I please,"

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:50.220
but use of the
 Wizard's Cane is not unlimited.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:51.400
What?

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:54.490
Burn! Burn! Burn!

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:59.630
You only saw the good things about it,
 and never looked at its flaws.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:10:04.890
Burn! Burn! Burn!

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:03.970
Your intense attraction to the cane 
you've desired for so many years...

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:07.960
Your conviction that it was the most 
powerful treasure of Nanana's Collection...

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:07.960
Burn, I said!

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:11.590
That forced you to abandon
 any doubt in the power of the cane.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:11.590
Burn! Burn!

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:16.550
Your overestimation of the cane's 
power brought about your defeat.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:13.560
Burn!

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.550
No... this can't be...

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:22.520
President Yuiga, you should 
have had Nanana-chan teach you

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:24.260
how to use the cane.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:29.230
But your guilt over what 
you did to us stopped you.

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:36.350
You were unable to keep your
 pride in your dream to the very end.

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:40.810
In other words, your dream
 didn't really mean that much to you.

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:49.940
<i>Pathetic. Absolutely pathetic.</i>

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:51.690
<i>Just die, Yama Juugo!</i>

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:54.680
<i>Where do you get off lecturing him like that?</i>

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:58.810
<i>You gave up your own beliefs long ago!</i>

00:10:58.810 --> 00:11:01.590
<i>You're just scum,
 blending in with the crowd!</i>

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:09.980
You're not going to hit me?

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:12.970
I don't think that's necessary.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.840
We both know I've won.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.070
Give me the cane.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:17.570
I'm afraid that's impossible.

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:19.090
Forgive me, my junior.

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:23.960
For the sake of Isshin's ambition, 
we can't give you the cane.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.420
Are you all right?

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:33.810
Where's Ibara-senpai?

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:34.800
She fled.

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:38.050
Why didn't you hit him?

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:40.610
Good question...

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.010
People don't lose their dreams!

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:50.770
<i>I just couldn't bear to hit
 someone with a dream that stupid.</i>

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:54.770
He really told you off, didn't he?

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.980
He sure did. I was speechless.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:01.970
But that Yama didn't seem like a bad person.

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:03.050
What?!

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:05.620
After he trashed Isshin-sama like that?!

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:20.130
Tensai-kun!

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.760
Hi there, Yuiga-dono.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:27.280
Fancy meeting you here.

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:29.560
What exactly are you?

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.270
Just a master detective.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:35.020
But right now,
 I'm a messenger of Ikkaku Shunjuu.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:36.980
What are you talking about?

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:38.650
Actually, when I cleared up

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:40.910
that government
 authority misunderstanding,

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:43.080
I asked for Ikkaku's assistance.

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:46.120
We made a deal that, 
though he didn't want to,

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.450
he would grant me one favor.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:50.070
What should we do? Break through?

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:53.240
No. You alone might be able to manage it,

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:55.150
but it's too much to ask of Yuu and me.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:56.940
If I give you this,

00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:00.550
will you guarantee the safety 
of myself and my companions?

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:03.980
A message from Ikkaku:

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:07.390
"I do business, but I do not steal."

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:08.780
His words.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.950
I'm sorry to call you here.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.100
Are you all right?

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:32.280
I hurt like hell.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:33.490
Forgive me.

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:34.950
I betrayed my junior

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:37.920
and wielded my power in vain, 
and this is how it ends?

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.690
Serves you right.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:41.790
Indeed.

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:45.610
And? What will you do now?

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:48.230
I'll go search for something else.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:51.500
A treasure from Nanana's
 Collection that'll achieve my goals.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.230
Well, I'll stop by the
 club room sometime.

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:01.030
No more betraying us.

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:04.100
I can't guarantee that.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:10.620
Hello, Juugo. I've been waiting for you.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:12.470
What do you mean, waiting?

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:15.660
Like hell you were! You abandoned me!

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:16.580
What's that?

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:21.790
Those guys kidnapped me, 
and you abandoned me.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:22.960
Why do you say that?

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:25.960
Aren't you working with the 
phantom thief troupe Matsuri?

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:27.810
What?

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:33.560
Why should I play along 
with your fake kidnapping?

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:36.810
W-Wait a minute! That's... um...

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:37.770
What?

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:39.980
How did you know?

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:43.500
I knew for sure when I forced my way into

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.480
room 202 and checked your cell phone.

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.610
What? You're kidding!

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:48.820
There's no way!

00:14:49.310 --> 00:14:52.400
You said you left the 
convenience store that night

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:55.190
because your phone vibrated, yes?

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:57.330
Yeah, but nobody believed me.

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:01.290
No. I believed you.

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:05.450
There were no messages
 or calls on your phone,

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:08.160
but there was an
 alarm set for that time.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:11.640
It was the time when the box containing

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:14.750
that jewel was dropped
 into the alley by parachute.

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:20.010
Juugo, you knew in advance

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:23.820
that the jewel would
 fall there at that time.

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:25.070
How did you know?

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:28.960
Because you knew
 everything about the crime Matsuri

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:30.650
was planning in advance!

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:34.120
So how did you find out about it?

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:37.370
Because you're working with Matsuri.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.820
And you took their plan
 out from under their noses.

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:42.500
Where's your proof?

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:45.630
I hacked your cell phone.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:49.410
I never expected those guys

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:53.470
to use a net-based
 SNS to concoct their plan.

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:56.310
When did you do that?!

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:59.490
While we were watching
 the convenience store video.

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:04.440
I downloaded a program to
 hack into your cell phone then.

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:07.200
Even when we were trapped in the ruins,

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:11.640
you contacted those two 
members of Matsuri for help.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:19.430
You're unbelievable.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:22.310
I never imagined
 you'd figure it out like this.

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:25.490
I saw through everything!

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:26.540
So?

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.750
Are you gonna hand me over to the police?

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:32.930
Juugo, every master detective needs a rival.

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:33.470
Huh?

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:36.500
Of course, it's best
 if the rival is a villain.

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:40.730
Specifically, a thoroughbred
 of evil, with superior physical ability

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:42.590
and a calculating mind...

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:44.560
And, of course, evil eyes!

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:48.260
Wait, you're not going to
 tell me to be all that, are you?

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:51.250
Nah. I wouldn't ask
 you to become one now.

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:53.230
Because you already are.

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:55.200
Huh? What do you mean?

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.550
At school, you sit next to me,

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:59.010
and starting tomorrow,

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:03.220
Daruku and I will move into 
room 203 of the Happy House.

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:04.670
You're going to...

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:13.250
That's the master detective, Ikkyuu Tensai!

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:15.710
Oh, shut up.

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:21.930
<b>Dad</b>

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:23.780
What?

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:26.440
<i>Yukihime told me what happened.</i>

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:28.650
<i>I just called because
 I liked what I heard.</i>

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:30.280
Is that so?

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:31.780
<i>How's the island?</i>

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:35.650
You exiled me to one weird island.

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:40.030
But, it did set me free from
 that out-of-date Matsuri business.

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:42.750
I'm living as I please.

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:45.750
<i>Glad to hear it.</i>

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:48.300
<i>So, now that you've turned your back</i>

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:50.480
<i>on Matsuri and live as you please,</i>

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:52.530
<i>what change of heart
 possessed you to get</i>

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:54.080
<i>Yukihime and Ibara involved?</i>

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:56.370
Nothing in particular.

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:01.350
<i>Didn't you say you wouldn't succeed me?</i>

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:02.970
That's right.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:05.490
You say you're noble thieves
 who steal from the wicked,

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:08.310
and who help people in 
trouble, but that's all bull.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.600
<i>I suppose so.</i>

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:13.730
<i>I know you don't like people, after all.</i>

00:18:15.890 --> 00:18:18.580
Don't just assume you know me, old man!

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:22.700
<i>Oh? I suppose you've already 
made a girlfriend or two, then?</i>

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:28.310
You better believe it! Girls love me!

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:32.880
This blonde girl I just met can't 
tear herself away from me.

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:35.090
<i>In a different way, though.</i>

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:37.650
<i>Oh? Impressive.</i>

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:41.220
<i>How much do you like her, then?</i>

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:43.020
<i>Spit it out.</i>

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:45.100
Huh? Why should I?

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:47.420
<i>You don't hate people, right?</i>

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:49.230
<i>So tell me.</i>

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:52.460
Well... I do respect her.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:55.190
I honestly think she's amazing.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:57.270
<i>But that's all, isn't it?</i>

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:59.460
<i>You don't love her so much</i>

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:02.550
<i>you'd throw away anything 
for her sake, right?</i>

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:04.830
It's not like I'm in love with her or...

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:07.540
<i>Then if she ever needed you,</i>

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:10.170
<i>would you be willing
 to do something for her?</i>

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:13.500
Well... I'd do whatever I could.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.840
<i>And how much is "whatever you could"?</i>

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:22.550
<i>In other words,
 you're still not able to love another.</i>

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:25.360
<i>That's why I don't believe 
you could save anyone.</i>

00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:30.270
<i>You have the strength,
 but you never use it for others.</i>

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:34.430
<i>It just means that no matter what I say,</i>

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:38.340
<i>you were never qualified to 
succeed me in the first place.</i>

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:39.520
You don't have to tell me that!

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:41.590
I'll die before I become a noble!

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:43.610
If you want Matsuri,
 you and your buddies

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:44.770
can keep it going!

00:19:44.770 --> 00:19:46.170
I won't do it!

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:47.560
I'll never do it!

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:49.120
I'd rather die!

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:02.800
Whoa! Is that even possible?

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:04.260
Damn you!

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:06.720
Stop following me!

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:13.190
Augh! This is infuriating!

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:23.880
Nice shot.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.370
Welcome back!

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:29.330
I'm home.

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:34.390
Hey, that's the
 Light-Up Lie Detector, isn't it?

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:39.370
Didn't you say you were
 going to use it to make some deal?

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:42.090
Yeah, but I ended up bringing it back.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:46.470
I handed her a fake,
 for a laugh, but she didn't notice.

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:51.180
You're actually pretty evil, aren't you?

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:52.780
I am not!

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:57.190
Sorry. I just thought
 it seemed like a waste,

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:59.300
so I didn't want to let it go.

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:00.690
Well, I guess it's okay.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.560
Um... what do you mean?

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:08.120
If it's you, I'm sure you'll 
use it to do something good.

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:23.480
I mean, you're going to
 find my killer for me, right?
